      "id": "sec-ph-14",
      "type": "reflection",
      "body": "Second chances do not arrive with trumpets or legal treaties. They arrive in the back of a provincial state bus, inside a canvas bag containing an old photograph and a tin of sweets. Forgiveness is not an intellectual concession that the past was acceptable; it is the humble recognition that the living are too fragile to be punished for the sins of the dead. When two people decide to drink tea together after twenty-four years of silence, they are not revising history; they are simply refusing to let their graves be dug while they are still breathing."
